.TH AD 1 "2026-09-10" "ad 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ad_vim \- animate a code diff in vim as if a human were typing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_vim
.RI [ options ]
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>
.br
.B ad_vim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-multi
.RI <old1:new1>
.RI <old2:new2>
\&...
.br
.B ad_vim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-replay
.RI <file>
.br
.B ad_vim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-git\-rev
.IR REV..REV
.RI <file>
[<file> ...]
.br
.B ad_vim
.B \-\-version
.br
.B ad_vim
.B \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_vim
opens the old version of a file in vim and animates the transformation into
the new version character by character. The cursor glides between change
locations with smooth ease-in-out acceleration, and only the actually-changed
characters are deleted and re-typed \(em surrounding text is never touched.

After the animation completes (or the user stops it), the buffer is a normal
vim buffer and can be edited, saved, or quit normally. By default the buffer
is marked as not modified so
.B :q
quits cleanly; use
.B \-\-keep\-dirty
to leave the buffer modified (then
.B :q!
is required).

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Core Options

.TP
.BR \-\-speed\  N \  \fR(\fB\-s\fR)
Speed multiplier.
.B 0.5
= half speed,
.B 2
= double speed,
.B 5
= 5x speed.
All timing delays are divided by this value.
Also settable via the
.B SPEED
variable in the config file (see CONFIGURATION section).

.TP
.BI \-\-output\  FILE \  \fR(\fB\-o\fR)
After the animation completes, write the buffer to
.I FILE
and quit vim. Also works with
.B q
(quit) \(em the buffer is written before stopping.

.TP
.B \-\-snapshot\ FILE
Alias for
.BR \-\-output .

.TP
.B \-\-no\-display
Run the animator headless (no terminal rendering). Useful for testing
and CI pipelines.

.TP
.B \-\-sync
Run without timers (synchronous mode). Useful for debugging timing issues.

.TP
.BI \-\-context\  N \  \fR(\fB\-c\fR)
Fold unchanged regions longer than 2*N lines, keeping N lines of context
around each hunk. Default: 0 (no folding).

.TP
.BI \-\-max\-hunk\-chars\  N
If a hunk has more than N changed characters, skip the char-by-char
animation and apply the entire hunk instantly.

.TP
.BI \-\-max\-line\-len\  N
Warn if any line exceeds N characters (char-level diff may be slow).
Default: 10000.

.TP
.BR \-\-scroll\  zz | zt | zb | none
Scroll the cursor to the specified position during animation:
.RS
.TP 4
.B zz
Center cursor on screen (default)
.TP 4
.B zt
Cursor at top of screen
.TP 4
.B zb
Cursor at bottom of screen
.TP 4
.B none
Don't force scroll
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-multi\  \fR(\fB\-m\fR)
Treat arguments as
.I old:new
pairs for multi-file animation. After finishing one file, the animation
transitions to the next.

.SS Compute / Diff Options

.TP
.BI \-\-precomputed\  FILE
Use a pre-computed diff from FILE (typically produced by
.BR ad_compute (1)).
Bypasses the in-vim patience diff entirely. By default
.B ad_vim
uses
.I bin/ad_compute
and falls back to the built-in vimscript LCS if not found.

.TP
.B \-\-word\-diff\  \fR(\fB\-w\fR)
Use word-level diff instead of char-level. Groups changes by word
(non-space sequences), producing more natural typing patterns.

.TP
.BR \-\-algorithm\  PATIENCE \  \fR(\fB\-a\fR)
Deprecated. Patience diff is now the only algorithm. The flag is accepted
for backward compatibility but has no effect.

.SS Pacing \(em Deletion

.TP
.BR \-\-delete\-pacing\  char | rapid\-eol | rapid\-identical | accel | word | instant | flash
Unified deletion strategy (default:
.BR word ).
.RS
.TP 4
.B char
One char at a time (no acceleration)
.TP 4
.B rapid\-eol
Rapid shot at end of line
.TP 4
.B rapid\-identical
Accelerate identical char runs (---, ===)
.TP 4
.B accel
Accelerate through long runs (slow\(->fast\(->slow)
.TP 4
.B word
Word-by-word with acceleration (default; char\(->word\(->rapid progression)
.TP 4
.B instant
All strategies enabled (fastest)
.TP 4
.B flash
Flash highlight then instant delete
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-delete\-speed\  slow | normal | fast | instant
Deletion speed multiplier (default:
.BR normal ).
.B fast
halves all delete delays;
.B instant
sets them to 1ms.

.TP
.BI \-\-delete\-threshold\  N
Minimum chars to trigger rapid/word modes (default: 3).

.SS Pacing \(em Insertion

.TP
.BR \-\-insert\-pacing\  char | word | accel
Unified insertion strategy (default:
.BR char ).
.RS
.TP 4
.B char
One char at a time (default)
.TP 4
.B word
Batch short words (<=8 chars) instantly
.TP 4
.B accel
Accelerate char-by-char inserts (slow\(->fast\(->pause)
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-insert\-speed\  slow | normal | fast
Insertion speed multiplier (default:
.BR normal ).
.B fast
halves TYPE_DELAY_MS and WORD_PAUSE_MS.

.SS Pacing \(em Timing Mode

.TP
.BR \-\-pacing\  uniform | adaptive | gaussian | review
Unified timing mode (default:
.BR uniform ).
.RS
.TP 4
.B uniform
Fixed delays, no jitter
.TP 4
.B adaptive
Slow down in complex regions
.TP 4
.B gaussian
Add human-like timing jitter
.TP 4
.B review
Pause every 5 lines in large hunks
.RE

.SS Highlighting and Display

.TP
.BR \-\-highlight\  none | inline | word | hunk
Unified highlight mode (default:
.BR none ).
.RS
.TP 4
.B none
No highlighting
.TP 4
.B inline
Paint freshly typed/deleted chars
.TP 4
.B word
Highlight the word at cursor before change
.TP 4
.B hunk
Highlight the entire hunk
.RE

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight\-color\  COLOR
Highlight group (default: DiffChange).

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight\-duration\-ms\  N
Highlight duration in ms (default: 1000).

.TP
.B \-\-dim\-unchanged\  \fR(\fB\-D\fR)
Dim unchanged anchor lines to draw the eye to changes.

.TP
.BI \-\-dim\-unchanged\-pct\  N
Dimming percentage 0-100 (default: 60).

.TP
.B \-\-sign\-column
Show +/- signs in the sign column during animation.

.TP
.B \-\-git\-blame\  \fR(\fB\-g\fR)
Echo git blame for the target line of each hunk.

.TP
.B \-\-diff\-stat
Show diff statistics overlay (changed/total lines).

.TP
.B \-\-diff\-highlight
Highlight modified lines with a subtle background.

.TP
.B \-\-bell
Ring terminal bell on potential errors.

.TP
.BR \-\-theme\  dark | light | high\-contrast \  \fR(\fB\-t\fR)
Color scheme for highlights.

.TP
.BI \-\-language\  LANG
Set vim filetype for syntax highlighting (default: auto-detect from file
extension).

.SS Postprocessing Layers

.TP
.B \-\-indent\-last
Delete leading whitespace LAST (prevents left shift when removing indent).

.TP
.B \-\-line\-delete\-in\-place
Delete whole lines on their own line (not joined to previous line first).

.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
In-place replacement instead of delete+insert.

.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer\  NAME\fR[:\fIARGS\fR]
Add a postprocess layer to the chain (after the default chain). The layer
is looked up in the search path
.RI ( bin/ ,
.IR layers/perl/ ;
override with
.BR \-\-ad\-layer\-path ).
Layer args follow the colon (use colons or spaces as separators).
Examples:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\-\-ad\-layer=ad_layer_reorder
\-\-ad\-layer=ad_layer_line_delete_in_place:\-\-mode=interleaved
\-\-ad\-layer NAME arg1 arg2
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer\-path\  DIR
Add DIR to the layer search path. May be given multiple times.

.TP
.B \-\-list\-layers
Print available layers and exit (delegates to
.BR ad_postprocess (1)).

.SS Cursor Movement

.TP
.BI \-\-cursor\-glide\-ms\  N
Glide duration between hunks (0=off, default: 0).

.TP
.BI \-\-cursor\-glide\-show\-intermediate\  0 | 1
Show lines during glide (default: 1).

.SS Distance-Based Speed

.TP
.BR \-\-distance\-speed\  adaptive | off
Adaptive speed based on hunk distance.

.TP
.BI \-\-distance\-threshold\  N
Lines above which speed increases (default: 10).

.TP
.BI \-\-distance\-fast\-mult\  F
Speed multiplier for long distances (default: 3.0).

.TP
.BI \-\-distance\-slow\-mult\  F
Speed multiplier for short distances (default: 0.5).

.SS Flash Mode

.TP
.BI \-\-flash\-pause\-ms\  N
Pause after highlight (default: 400).

.TP
.BI \-\-flash\-highlight\-ms\  N
Highlight duration (default: 300).

.SS Git Options

.TP
.B \-\-replay\  \fR(\fB\-r\fR)
Animate git history for the given file(s). For each commit in the range,
extracts the old version and animates the transformation to the next commit.

.TP
.BI \-\-git\-rev\  REV..REV \  \fR(\fB\-R\fR)
Animate a git commit range using
.I REV..REV
syntax (e.g.
.BR HEAD~3..HEAD ).

.SS Startup and Logging

.TP
.B \-\-startup\-pause
Show config + help before starting.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-startup\-pause
Skip startup delay and messages, start immediately.

.TP
.B \-\-startup\-feedback\  \fR(\fB\-F\fR)
Show progress in status line during diff computation.

.TP
.B \-\-step\-mode
Space advances one op at a time (starts paused).

.TP
.B \-\-annotate
Write annotated ops with
.B # old:
and
.B # new:
context comments before each hunk to
.IR /tmp/ad_vim_ops_annotated_<pid>.tsv .
The comments show the text content before/after each bundle of delete
or insert ops, making it easier to understand the diff structure
without watching the full animation. The annotated ops are also used
for the animation itself (the animator ignores comment lines).

.TP
.B \-\-keep\-dirty
Leave buffer modified; require
.B :q!
to quit (default: off).

.TP
.B \-\-no\-vimrc\  \fR(\fB\-N\fR)
Don't load user's ~/.vimrc (isolated vim, default: off).

.TP
.BI \-\-preset\  NAME \  \fR(\fB\-p\fR)
Apply named preset:
.RS
.TP 4
.B fast\-delete
\-\-delete\-pacing word \-\-delete\-speed fast
.TP 4
.B review
\-\-pacing review \-\-highlight hunk \-\-dim\-unchanged
.TP 4
.B demo
\-\-pacing gaussian \-\-speed 0.7 \-\-highlight inline
.TP 4
.B ai\-code
\-\-highlight inline \-\-pacing adaptive
.RE

.TP
.BI \-\-log\-mode\  1 | 2
Generate a log file without starting vim.

.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file\  FILE
Write log to FILE (default: diffvim.log).

.TP
.B \-\-no\-log\-timing
Disable timing info in log output.

.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose logging to /tmp/diffvim-debug.log.

.SS Informational

.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run\  \fR(\fB\-d\fR)
Print diff hunks without launching vim.

.TP
.B \-\-version\  \fR(\fB\-V\fR)
Print version and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-help\  \fR(\fB\-h\fR)
Show help and exit.

.SH CONTROLS
During animation, the following keys are active in vim normal mode:

.SS Basic Controls
.TP
.B <Space>
Pause / resume the animation. In
.B \-\-step\-mode ,
advances one char op instead.
.TP
.B n
Skip current hunk: apply all remaining character operations instantly,
then pause for review.
.TP
.B b
Back to previous hunk: revert the buffer to the state before the
current hunk started and replay it from the beginning.
.TP
.B q
Stop the animation. By default the buffer is then marked as not modified
so
.B :q
quits cleanly. Use
.B \-\-keep\-dirty
to require
.B :q!
instead.

.SS Speed Controls
.TP
.B +
Speed up: multiply the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B \-
Slow down: divide the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B =
Reset speed to 1.0x.

.SS Multi-File Navigation (only with \-\-multi)
.TP
.B ]
Next file. Applies all remaining hunks instantly and loads the next file pair.
.TP
.B [
Previous file. Loads the previous file pair.

.SS Git Replay Controls (only with \-\-replay or \-\-git\-rev)
.TP
.B )
Next commit in the replay sequence.
.TP
.B (
Previous commit in the replay sequence.

.SS Display
.TP
.B ?
Show in-vim help.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.B ad_vim
reads configuration from a file at startup, with CLI flags overriding
per-invocation. There are NO environment variables read directly by the
launcher.

.SS Config file location
Following the XDG Base Directory Specification, the config file is at:
.PP
.RS
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ad/config
.RE
.PP
(defaults to ~/.config/ad/config when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset)

.SS Precedence
.PP
.RS
.nf
1. /etc/ad/config        (system-wide defaults, lowest priority)
2. ~/.config/ad/config   (user config)
3. CLI flags             (per-invocation, highest priority)
.fi
.RE

.SS Config file format
The config file is sourced as bash. Set variables using UPPER_CASE names
(without any AD_ prefix). Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# ~/.config/ad/config
DELETE_PACING=word
INSERT_PACING=char
PACING=uniform
INDENT_LAST=1
CURSOR_GLIDE_MS=100
HIGHLIGHT_MODE=inline
.fi
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic Usage
.PP
.nf
ad_vim old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Speed Control
.PP
.nf
# Half speed for a presentation
ad_vim \-\-speed 0.5 old.py new.py

# 3x speed for quick review
ad_vim \-\-speed 3 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Output
.PP
.nf
# Write result to file and quit
ad_vim \-\-output result.py old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Display Options
.PP
.nf
# Center cursor, highlight hunks, fold unchanged regions
ad_vim \-\-scroll zz \-\-highlight hunk \-\-context 0 old.py new.py

# High-contrast theme
ad_vim \-\-theme high\-contrast old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Diff Options
.PP
.nf
# Word-level diff
ad_vim \-\-word\-diff old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Unified Options
.PP
.nf
# Deletion strategy: word-by-word with acceleration
ad_vim \-\-delete\-pacing word old.py new.py

# Fast deletion for large refactors
ad_vim \-\-delete\-pacing instant \-\-delete\-speed fast old.py new.py

# Insertion strategy: batch short words
ad_vim \-\-insert\-pacing word old.py new.py

# Timing: human-like jitter
ad_vim \-\-pacing gaussian old.py new.py

# Timing: pause every 5 lines for review
ad_vim \-\-pacing review old.py new.py

# Highlight freshly typed/deleted chars
ad_vim \-\-highlight inline old.py new.py

# Highlight the entire hunk before animating
ad_vim \-\-highlight hunk old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Postprocess Layers
.PP
.nf
# Delete whole lines in place (not joined to previous)
ad_vim \-\-line\-delete\-in\-place old.py new.py

# Add a custom layer with arguments
ad_vim \-\-ad\-layer=ad_layer_line_delete_in_place:\-\-mode=interleaved old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Buffer State After Animation
.PP
.nf
# Default: ':q' quits cleanly (buffer marked not modified)
ad_vim old.py new.py

# Keep buffer modified; ':q!' required to quit
ad_vim \-\-keep\-dirty old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Multi-file Animation
.PP
.nf
ad_vim \-\-multi old1.py:new1.py old2.py:new2.py
.fi

.SS Git Integration
.PP
.nf
# Replay history of a file
ad_vim \-\-replay src/main.py

# Using \-\-git\-rev syntax for a specific range
ad_vim \-\-git\-rev HEAD~3..HEAD src/main.py

# Show git blame during animation
ad_vim \-\-git\-blame old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Debugging
.PP
.nf
# Dry run (print ops without launching vim)
ad_vim \-\-dry\-run old.py new.py

# Verbose logging
ad_vim \-\-debug old.py new.py
cat /tmp/diffvim-debug.log
.fi

.SS Vim Plugin
.PP
.nf
# Inside an existing vim session:
:Diffvim old.py new.py
:Diffvim old.py new.py tabnew
.fi

